UCanDrop on Ubuntu
==================

This package installs the client, receiver completion modules, radio helpers,
and a native OWL binary under /usr/lib/ucandrop. It has no maintainer scripts
that enable or start a service, and receiving is disabled after installation.

The runtime/radio interface is stable inside that tree: the client invokes
/usr/lib/ucandrop/radio/omdrop-discoverable and
/usr/lib/ucandrop/radio/send-to-peer, and both helpers find
/usr/lib/ucandrop/radio/owl beside themselves. The package's polkit and
NetworkManager fragments are installed from the matching files in packaging/;
no legacy /usr/lib/omdrop path is used.

As the normal desktop user, run:

    ucandrop setup
    ucandrop doctor --json
    ucandrop on 1h

The first command creates the per-user receiver configuration. The second
checks the environment. The third opens a one-hour receive window.
Use `ucandrop off` to close it early. Installing this package requires no
source compilation and no invocation of tools/install.sh.

The package targets Ubuntu 26.04 with NetworkManager and a supported Wi-Fi
adapter. The radio backend reports unsupported or unverified hardware instead
of claiming that every adapter can provide AirDrop service.
